   "subject": "Confidence intervals for parameter estimates",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear unmarked users,<div><br></div><div>I want to calculate 95% CI for the parameter estimates in a distsamp model. The output when I call the model includes the z-score, p, estimate and standard error. Can I just use the standard error to obtain the intervals (Estimate <span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">± </span>SE x 1.96)? I realize this is a question related to statistics but I have only calculated CI in very basic scenarios (CI for means that I calculate). I just want to be completely sure that I am doing this correctly. Thank you very much in advance for any input and apologies for the very basic question.</div><div><br></div><div>Sincerely,</div><div><br></div><div>Lucas</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
